{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Speak now.</b> Speak now <b>in the ears of the people,</b> for there is no delay in the matter, since they will depart entirely. But in the case of the plagues that came beforehand, had the Egyptians not lent to them, they would say to them: return to me what I lent you — when they see Pharaoh refusing to grant them permission to leave permanently." "<b>And they shall ask, each man.</b> What the Holy One, blessed be He, had promised — and afterward they went out with great substance, in the manner of borrowing and not in the manner of gift, so that the Egyptians would be eager to pursue after them. And one may say: וישאלו means a pure gift, as in 'ask of me and I will give,' etc." "<b>From his fellow.</b> Now were the Egyptians fellows to Israel? Rather, it teaches that after the plagues they were like fellows and friends to Israel, to lend them their vessels." "<b>Vessels of silver and vessels of gold.</b> In place of what Israel left behind — their houses and their fields and their vessels that they could not carry with them — for Israel did have inheritances in Egypt, as it is written: 'and they took hold in it.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:59.782493543Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}